://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-26T18:17:53Z","updated_at":"2025-05-26T18:17:53Z","body":"Thanks!\r\n\r\nThe black icon on the dark-blue background also stuck out to me as a visibility issue. Given it's the existing behavior for the editor (including other parts of the interface as you pointed out), and the main purpose of this PR is to provide the shortcut to the editor settings via the popup menu, I think it makes sense to save the color styling for a future PR instead.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2910392247/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2916631539","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106231#issuecomment-2916631539","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106231","id":2916631539,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6t2EPz","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T14:49:01Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T14:49:01Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2916631539/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3705508273","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106231#issuecomment-3705508273","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106231","id":3705508273,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7c3ZGx","user":{"login":"inhalt120g","id":106015575,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlGrVw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106015575?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/inhalt120g","html_url":"https://github.com/inhalt120g","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inhalt120g/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inhalt120g/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inhalt120g/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inhalt120g/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inhalt120g/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inhalt120g/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inhalt120g/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inhalt120g/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inhalt120g/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-02T14:45:19Z","updated_at":"2026-01-02T14:45:19Z","body":"As someone who makes lots of movies… When I first saw this feature, I thought it's a great improvement but after using this button for a while, I have to say I really don't like it.\r\n\r\nThe main problem is that every time I want to enable / disable Movie Maker, I have to click twice in order to do that (first click on the button, then tick / untick the box). The dropdown menu is just slowing things down. It's needlessly adding yet another button that has to be clicked. Before, it was just a simple toggle which was simple and fast.\r\n\r\nAs is, it's also introducing inconsistencies. Right next to it, there is the Remote Deploy button, which unlike the current Movie Maker button does not offer you to open something like Build / Export settings (and why should it).\r\n\r\nAll the problems it tries to solve are better solved in other ways, for example in the case of #11541 : keep a File Explorer / Finder / whatever window with the target directory open and after Godot generates the file just rename the file in the file manager as you see fit. (chances are you'll have to open that folder in the file manager later anyway if you want to use the file, and it makes no difference if you input the name in the file manager or Godot)","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3705508273/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3705804000","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106231#issuecomment-3705804000","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106231","id":3705804000,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7c4hTg","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-02T17:04:52Z","updated_at":"2026-01-02T17:13:40Z","body":"> It's needlessly adding yet another button that has to be clicked. Before, it was just a simple toggle which was simple and fast.\r\n\r\nI wouldn't say it's \"needless\", necessarily, since it does make it much quicker to access the Movie Maker settings for those who need it. I do agree though that the extra click is annoying. I've faced a similar issue with the Run Current Scene button when working on my XR project; it always asks me if I want to run in Regular or XR mode, even though when I'm in the editor I always want to run in Regular.\r\n\r\n> Right next to it, there is the Remote Deploy button, which unlike the current Movie Maker button does not offer you to open something like Build / Export settings (and why should it).\r\n\r\nHonestly this seems to me like something where a menu item to open those settings could make sense, if someone did want to investigate options related to the options that button provides.\r\n\r\n> All the problems it tries to solve are better solved in other ways, for example in the case of https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11541 : keep a File Explorer / Finder / whatever window with the target directory open and after Godot generates the file just rename the file in the file manager as you see fit\r\n\r\nI suppose this would work, but it seems like a rather \"low-tech\" solution to me. The aim with the proposal and PR were to prevent the user from needing to scroll through Project Settings or work with other applications in order to record multiple videos. There is a PR open that allows the editor to detect when the file it plans to write the output video to already exists, and use a different filename to avoid overwriting (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/92067); perhaps we could push for that to be updated and merged in 4.7.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBased on this, there are a few ideas I have:\r\n\r\n- Something like what I tried in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104954 could be revisited; the main Movie Maker button goes back to being a simple toggle, but it has a \"side button\" that provides quick access to Movie Maker-related options.\r\n  - Alternatively, perhaps left-clicking the Movie Maker button could toggle its status, whereas right-clicking (or holding on touch screens) could display the dropdown menu.\r\n    - This would be inconsistent with other buttons' behaviors that always pop up their dropdown menu, though...\r\n- When Movie Maker mode is enabled but there is already a file at the filepath it plans to write to, the Movie Maker icon could display a small warning indicator.\r\n  - The PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/92067 would also address this issue.\r\n  - The user could be asked for a destination filepath to save the movie to via a pop-up FileDialog, once they close the game.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3705804000/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]